{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SGJB458cktmBZudBs3n4X5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t.\\\" leftpad.3 - Copyright (c) 2019, Sijmen J. Mulder (see LICENSE.md)\n2\t.Dd June 25, 2019\n3\t.Dt LEFTPAD 3\n4\t.Os\n5\t.Sh NAME\n6\t.Nm leftpad\n7\t.Nd pad a string to a desired length\n8\t.Sh SYNOPSIS\n9\t.In stddef.h\n10\t.In leftpad.h\n11\t.Ft size_t\n12\t.Fo leftpad\n13\t.Fa \"const char *str\"\n14\t.Fa \"const char *padding\"\n15\t.Fa \"size_t min_len\"\n16\t.Fa \"char *dest\" \n17\t.Fa \"size_t dest_sz\"\n18\t.Fc\n19\t.Sh DESCRIPTION\n20\t.Fn leftpad\n21\twrites\n22\t.Fa padding\n23\t.Po\n24\tor spaces if\n25\t.Dv NULL\n26\tor empty\n27\t.Pc\n28\tand\n29\t.Fa str\n30\t.Po\n31\tif not\n32\t.Dv NULL\n33\t.Pc\n34\tto\n35\t.Fa dest ,\n36\twhere\n37\t.Fa padding\n38\tis repeated or cut off as needed to make for a minimum final string length of\n39\t.Fa min_len .\n40\t.Pp\n41\tIf\n42\t.Fa dest\n43\tis\n44\t.Dv NULL\n45\tor\n46\t.Fa dest_sz\n47\t0, nothing is written. Otherwise, up to\n48\t.Fa dest_sz\n49\tcharacters are written, including the\n50\t.Ql \\e0\n51\tterminator, possibly truncating the output.\n52\t.Sh RETURN VALUES\n53\tThe length of the output string.\n54\tIf less than\n55\t.Fa dest_sz ,\n56\tthe output has not been truncated.\n57\t.Sh EXAMPLES\n58\tPad the string\n59\t.Qq 5581\n60\tto 16 characters, assuming\n61\t.Va buf\n62\tis a character array of sufficient size:\n63\t.Bd -literal -offset indent\n64\tleftpad(\"5581\", \"*\", 16, buf, sizeof(buf));\n65\tputs(buf); /* outputs: ************5581 */\n66\t.Ed\n67\t.Pp\n68\tUsing\n69\t.Fn leftpad\n70\tto repeat a string:\n71\t.Bd -literal -offset indent\n72\tleftpad(NULL, \"_-\", 40, buf, sizeof(buf));\n73\tputs(buf); /* outputs: _-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_- */\n74\t.Ed\n75\t.Pp\n76\tCalling\n77\t.Fn leftpad\n78\twithout a buffer to find out the required buffer size:\n79\t.Bd -literal -offset indent\n80\tsize_t len = leftpad(some_str, \" \", 10);\n81\tchar *buf = malloc(len+1); /* +1 for terminating NUL */\n82\tleftpad(some_str, \" \", 10, buf, len+1);\n83\t.Ed\n84\t.Sh SEE ALSO\n85\t.Xr leftpad 1\n86\t.Sh AUTHORS\n87\t.An Sijmen J. Mulder\n88\t.Aq Mt ik@sjmulder.nl\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a9f183c-e816-4be5-ba96-4e4e177de90c","uuid":"e1b8e246-13a0-4440-b87e-bddaa255d898","timestamp":"2026-06-03T09:33:42.842Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-31062124/harvest-crust-qKUA0p/project/c_src/leftpad.3","content":".\\\" leftpad.3 - Copyright (c) 2019, Sijmen J. Mulder (see LICENSE.md)\n.Dd June 25, 2019\n.Dt LEFTPAD 3\n.Os\n.Sh NAME\n.Nm leftpad\n.Nd pad a string to a desired length\n.Sh SYNOPSIS\n.In stddef.h\n.In leftpad.h\n.Ft size_t\n.Fo leftpad\n.Fa \"const char *str\"\n.Fa \"const char *padding\"\n.Fa \"size_t min_len\"\n.Fa \"char *dest\" \n.Fa \"size_t dest_sz\"\n.Fc\n.Sh DESCRIPTION\n.Fn leftpad\nwrites\n.Fa padding\n.Po\nor spaces if\n.Dv NULL\nor empty\n.Pc\nand\n.Fa str\n.Po\nif not\n.Dv NULL\n.Pc\nto\n.Fa dest ,\nwhere\n.Fa padding\nis repeated or cut off as needed to make for a minimum final string length of\n.Fa min_len .\n.Pp\nIf\n.Fa dest\nis\n.Dv NULL\nor\n.Fa dest_sz\n0, nothing is written. Otherwise, up to\n.Fa dest_sz\ncharacters are written, including the\n.Ql \\e0\nterminator, possibly truncating the output.\n.Sh RETURN VALUES\nThe length of the output string.\nIf less than\n.Fa dest_sz ,\nthe output has not been truncated.\n.Sh EXAMPLES\nPad the string\n.Qq 5581\nto 16 characters, assuming\n.Va buf\nis a character array of sufficient size:\n.Bd -literal -offset indent\nleftpad(\"5581\", \"*\", 16, buf, sizeof(buf));\nputs(buf); /* outputs: ************5581 */\n.Ed\n.Pp\nUsing\n.Fn leftpad\nto repeat a string:\n.Bd -literal -offset indent\nleftpad(NULL, \"_-\", 40, buf, sizeof(buf));\nputs(buf); /* outputs: _-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_- */\n.Ed\n.Pp\nCalling\n.Fn leftpad\nwithout a buffer to find out the required buffer size:\n.Bd -literal -offset indent\nsize_t len = leftpad(some_str, \" \", 10);\nchar *buf = malloc(len+1); /* +1 for terminating NUL */\nleftpad(some_str, \" \", 10, buf, len+1);\n.Ed\n.Sh SEE ALSO\n.Xr leftpad 1\n.Sh AUTHORS\n.An Sijmen J. Mulder\n.Aq Mt ik@sjmulder.nl\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
